{
 "duration": 25.453,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "The waterfall had frozen into a wall of ice, and Tom walked right up to it for the photo.",
   "start": 0.4,
   "end": 5.646
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a chunk broke off above him and hit the rocks a few feet away.",
   "start": 6.446,
   "end": 10.027
  },
  {
   "text": "Frozen waterfalls can drop ice without warning, most of all when the sun warms them.",
   "start": 10.827,
   "end": 15.661
  },
  {
   "text": "Water can still run under the ice at the base.",
   "start": 16.461,
   "end": 18.892
  },
  {
   "text": "Take the photo from a distance, and stay off the ice.",
   "start": 19.692,
   "end": 22.598
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next winter hike.",
   "start": 23.398,
   "end": 25.253
  }
 ],
